  "summary": "Lightwell Security Advisory: jackson-core 2.17.3.rhlw-00005",
  "details": "Red Hat Lightwell has released com.fasterxml.jackson.core:jackson-core 2.17.3.rhlw-00005 with backported fixes for CVE-2026-18401, CVE-2026-68494, CVE-2026-89407, and CVE-2026-89425.\n\nCVE-2026-18401: jackson-core: Number length constraint bypass in non-blocking (async) JSON parser leads to potential denial of service\n\nCVE-2026-68494: jackson-core: Async parser maxNumberLength bypass via chunked digit accumulation (incomplete fix for CVE-2026-18401 / GHSA-72hv-8253-57qq)\n\nCVE-2026-89407: jackson-core: quadratic backtracking in NumberInput.PATTERN_FLOAT via looksLikeValidNumber() enables ReDoS\n\nCVE-2026-89425: jackson-core: UTF8DataInputJsonParser._reportInvalidToken() does not honor maxErrorTokenLength, allowing unbounded StringBuilder growth\n\nThis patched artifact is a drop-in replacement for com.fasterxml.jackson.core:jackson-core 2.17.3 from Maven Central.",
